BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Center Stage — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261128T150000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261128T160000
DTSTAMP:20261126T213814Z
UID:69850be012f059b844ffddf2d11b@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:After a string of memorable performances as strong-willed\, be
 autiful\, and virtuous women\, the actress Ruan Lingyu committed suicide i
 n 1935\, at the age of twenty-four. Stanley Kwan’s innovative film goes 
 far beyond the traditional biopic to offer up several strata of “reality
 \,” “reenactment\,” and “cinema.” Detailed re-creations of scene
 s from the actress’s too-short life combine with documentary interviews 
 of her contemporaries\, actual footage from her existing silent films\, an
 d even discussions between star Maggie Cheung\, Kwan\, and other cast memb
 ers. Like a Russian doll\, Center Stage reveals a Modernist take on the wa
 ys in which cinema and culture create an actress\, a legend\, and a woman.
 \nCategory: Films\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/ev
 ent/331167-film-screening-center-stage
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331167-film-screening-center-
 stage
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
