DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261204T170000
DTSTAMP:20261126T213814Z
UID:d34069c751704f0264a7e655da2b@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\, Open to the Public\,Providence\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Presented in conjunction with the symposium Queering the Algor
 ithm: Surveillance\, Resistance\, and the Future of AI \, this weeklong ex
 hibition showcases three single-channel HD video installations by artist\,
  writer\, filmmaker\, and theorist Zach Blas . While much of the current p
 ublic discourse on machine learning foc uses on its potential for bias\, B
 las’s work pushes deeper into the systemic architecture of the digital w
 orld—moving beside and beyond critiques of how models encode heteronorma
 tive and patriarchal biases or erase non-binary identities through rigid d
 ata classification to actively reimagine and “queer” the code . Works 
 on Display (9:00 AM – 5:00 PM): im here to learn so :)))))) (\nCategory:
   Open to the Public\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/live/even
 ts/344121-exhibition-videos-by-zach-blas
LOCATION:Carriage House\, Carriage House
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.brown.edu/live/events/344121-exhibition-videos-by-zach-
 blas
